course: dictionary
lesson: 6564
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Nickel is one of them: it can name a coin or a metal. Context, the words around it, tells you which meaning the writer wants. Look for clues before you choose.
explain: «A dime (10 cents) is smaller than a nickel (5 cents).» The words cents, dime and smaller are clues about money, so here a nickel is a coin worth 5 cents. Ask yourself: does the sentence talk about money, or about something a magnet could pick up?
explain: «The outer core is liquid iron and nickel.» The words iron and liquid tell you this is about a substance. Try the coin meaning in the sentence: "liquid iron and a coin" makes no sense, so here nickel is the metal.
fact: Nickel can mean a coin worth 5 cents in the USA and Canada.
fact: Nickel can also mean a hard, silver-coloured metal, and a chemical element.
fact: «In the USA, 100 cents make $1; a quarter is 25 cents, a dime 10 cents, a nickel 5 cents and a penny 1 cent.»
fact: Magnets pull on nickel, along with iron and cobalt.
fact: Nickel metal is used in coins, batteries and steel.
exercise: «A dime (10 cents) is smaller than a nickel (5 cents).» In this sentence, what is a nickel? | A metal that magnets pull on | A parking meter | A kind of snack | *A coin worth 5 cents
exercise: «The outer core is liquid iron and nickel.» In this sentence, what is nickel? | A liquid you can drink | A tool for mending bikes | A coin worth 5 cents | *A hard, silver-coloured metal
exercise: «In the USA, 100 cents make $1; a quarter is 25 cents, a dime 10 cents, a nickel 5 cents and a penny 1 cent.» How many nickels make 25 cents? | 4 | 2 | *5 | 10
test: «The Earth's inner core is a solid ball of iron and nickel.» What clue tells you that nickel here is a metal? | The word cents | The word penny | *The word iron beside it | The word dime
test: Nickel the metal is hard and silver-coloured. Which fact about it is true? | *Magnets can pull on it | It is a coin worth 25 cents | It is soft and turns to liquid in your pocket | It is a type of bread
exam: Sam paid for his snack with a nickel. What does nickel mean here? | A type of magnet | *A coin worth 5 cents | A silver spoon | A metal used in batteries
